OL,3,GNEWSAPlans progress but 550 flats
OL,4,Ademolition 'not imminent'
OL,5,
OL,6,FResidents of eight Brighton tower
OL,7,Fblocks set to be knocked down because
OL,8,Fthey no longer meet safety standards
OL,9,Fhave been told the demolition is "not
OL,10,Fimminent" but is moving forward.
OL,12,FBrighton and Hove City Council (BHCC)
OL,13,Fpreviously agreed to demolish Falcon
OL,14,FCourt, Heron Court, Kestrel Court,
OL,15,FKingfisher Court and Swallow Court in
OL,16,FWhitehawk, Dudeney Lodge and Nettleton
OL,17,FCourt in Hollingdean and St James's
OL,18,FHouse in Kemptown.
OL,20,FThe next step is that BHCC will issue
OL,21,Finitial demolition notices to residents
OL,22,Fof the 554 flats.
OL,23,APub: 10-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,330,320,200,140,0,100
